arget_id":"c40c-f87e-704b-4c3e"},{"link_uuid":"c2310f94-8531-4c41-acbb-5e9e001b66b7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ad35-76ef-30e8-43c9"},{"link_uuid":"3db744fd-3b40-4078-84ca-d7d4f5aa7c01","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"009c-3838-6e9a-4ab0"},{"link_uuid":"4e72616c-e79b-4b03-adcb-310777a0d988","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d08f-7b49-2ec0-4866"},{"link_uuid":"fe978013-89a6-464d-8544-f96f57af6b93","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2b94-7a39-dd6f-4ea2"},{"link_uuid":"b5476131-f0fd-4277-88a3-affd4c070a8d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2ecd-7bd2-4020-4dce"},{"link_uuid":"422c71b3-0dcb-48f8-a0df-3bfa7e2c2e9f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"de73-e0d4-cf50-425d"},{"link_uuid":"69c38bfd-38d4-44aa-93c9-73a3050af2ef","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e0ab-389c-55b9-46fd"},{"link_uuid":"d23c8855-9d1e-435a-b62b-d8b0d6257d1f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"103b-66c9-edf4-4b8a"},{"link_uuid":"d453fbd7-27b4-491d-b5f5-140f1348ba92","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"542a-74ca-0d0d-4672"},{"link_uuid":"b22b3b18-0984-4d04-91f7-2b10cbe9a998","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cda9-36ea-97b2-4fac"},{"link_uuid":"9d0bc3b3-6c5a-4853-a4eb-91e3ad88eb4e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1f3a-7778-be76-4b39"},{"link_uuid":"bc4919b6-e452-4efc-91eb-ab3eb93bd837","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"bae5-c0fc-ced6-42ab"},{"link_uuid":"48b811b0-cc3d-4337-b633-cab33b65d56c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5917-7451-92d1-409c"},{"link_uuid":"9835a612-f5aa-4b69-a486-cb53702510d8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"01f8-acea-0ab5-4b13"},{"link_uuid":"c2678265-da56-4f80-8fb1-a8dc96e42079","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a8d6-c5bf-48cd-48bd"},{"link_uuid":"b54599dc-940c-4a8e-b800-775889097cc0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1be6-99f4-f337-4ab2"},{"link_uuid":"dfe92fe8-4aa3-457a-82a0-7674dc168880","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d2a1-e18a-f366-4c7d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_keygen_heldout.py:1-7` — Preserve independent key-generation coverage. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_kind_vocabulary.py:1-14` — Preserve the closed operation-certificate kind set. Consumer: op-cert maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py:1-17` — Preserve local verification bound to the configured environment. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a.py:1-13` — Preserve resolution of the signer's own public key. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py:1-20, 58-64` — Preserve removal of private-key material from child-process environments. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py:1-23` — Preserve the injectable operation-certificate producer seam. Consumer: op-cert maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py:1-15, 141-145` — Preserve refusal to sign without a matching public counterpart. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_rollback_heldout.py:1-12` — Preserve independent rollback-safety coverage. Consumer: security and deployment maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py:270-286` — Preserve signing-service authentication, validation, and response contract. Consumer: op-cert service maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_integrity_heldout.py:1-12` — Preserve independent service-integrity coverage. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_storage_heldout.py:1-12` — Preserve independent storage coverage. Consumer: op-cert maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_storage.py:1-12` — Preserve operation-certificate persistence and lookup semantics. Consumer: op-cert maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py:1-15, 100-104, 169-173, 351-359` — Preserve OpenAI-compatible request shape, parsing, error, and capability behavior. Consumer: provider maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py:1-23` — Preserve Responses API request/response compatibility. Consumer: provider maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py:1-15` — Preserve immutable operation snapshot semantics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_oracle_grade_split.py:1-11` — Preserve the oracle-grade distinction. Consumer: evaluation maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py:1-12` — Preserve published output-schema completeness and validity. Consumer: MCP API maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py:697-703` — Preserve overlap-judging edge behavior. Consumer: evaluation maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_keygen_heldout.py tests/unit/test_opcert_kind_vocabulary.py tes